      "writtenOn": "2026-01-15T20:22:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can move to CONFIG_INSPECTION or CONFIG_ANALYZER.\nI don\u0027t see many lines of code under these two macros.\nDo you know is there any specific use case of them?\nI want to avoid that the new print disrupts existing functionality.\nIf no specific use case, I can move the code under CONFIG_INSPECTION.",
      "parentUuid": "b590e118_3c88dc0b",
      "revId": "bbe4f782bfe1dc41dac2fa6c9caa1d16fea0ffa6",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23fc04c3_fdb63b7a",
        "filename": "build/cmake/aom_config_defaults.cmake",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 147,
      "author": {
        "id": 5020
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-15T22:15:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I can move to CONFIG_INSPECTION or CONFIG_ANALYZER.\n\u003e I don\u0027t see many lines of code under these two macros.\n\u003e Do you know is there any specific use case of them?\n\u003e I want to avoid that the new print disrupts existing functionality.\n\u003e If no specific use case, I can move the code under CONFIG_INSPECTION.\n\n(I think I meant `CONFIG_ACCOUNTING` instead of `CONFIG_ANALYZER` above.) They were meant to add accounting in the arithmetic decoder (`CONFIG_ACCOUNTING`) and supply this data (if enabled) as well as frame/block level, etc. data (`CONFIG_INSPECTION`) to a bitstream analyzer, similar to VQAnalyzer. With `-DCONFIG_INSPECTION\u003d1` an `inspect` binary will be created that dumps this information. Try it out:\n\n```\nUsage: ./inspect src_filename \u003coptions\u003e\n\nOptions:\n            --limit\u003d\u003carg\u003e               Stop decoding after n frames\n  -A,       --all                       Dump All\n  -x,       --compress                  Compress JSON using RLE\n  -a,       --accounting                Dump Accounting\n  -bs,       --blockSize                Dump Block Size\n  -ts,       --transformSize            Dump Transform Size\n  -tt,       --transformType            Dump Transform Type\n  -m,       --mode                      Dump Mode\n  -uvm,       --uv_mode                 Dump UV Intra Prediction Modes\n  -mm,       --motion_mode              Dump Motion Modes\n  -ct,       --compound_type            Dump Compound Types\n  -s,       --skip                      Dump Skip\n  -f,       --filter                    Dump Filter\n  -c,       --cdef                      Dump CDEF\n  -df,       --dualFilterType           Dump Dual Filter Type\n  -cfl,       --chroma_from_luma        Dump Chroma from Luma Alphas\n  -r,       --referenceFrame            Dump Reference Frame\n  -mv,       --motionVectors            Dump Motion Vectors\n  -dq,       --delta_q                  Dump QIndex\n  -si,       --seg_id                   Dump Segment ID\n  -ibc,       --intrabc                 Dump If IntraBC Is Used\n  -plt,       --palette                 Dump Palette Size\n  -uvp,       --uv_palette              Dump UV Palette Size\n  -h,       --help                      Help\n  -snt \u003carg\u003e, --skip_non_transform\u003d\u003carg\u003e\n                                        Skip is counted as a non transform.\n  -comb \u003carg\u003e, --combined\u003d\u003carg\u003e         combinining parameters into one output.\n```",
      "parentUuid": "df80e13f_50300893",
      "revId": "bbe4f782bfe1dc41dac2fa6c9caa1d16fea0ffa6",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
